---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
import { getSitePage, REVIEWED_DATE, REVIEWED_ISO } from "../data/sitePages";

const page = getSitePage("/accessibility/");
---

<BaseLayout
  title={page.title}
  description={page.description}
  alternateMd="/accessibility/index.md"
  pageType="WebPage"
  dateModified={REVIEWED_ISO}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Accessibility" }]} />
  <section class="tight">
    <div class="wrap narrow prose">
      <h1>Accessibility statement</h1>
      <p class="small">Last reviewed: {REVIEWED_DATE}</p>
      <p class="lead" style="font-size:1.05rem;color:var(--ink-2)">
        This statement describes the accessibility work done on this site, the barriers we know remain, and how to
        tell us when a page or document does not work for you. It is written for people using keyboards, screen
        readers, zoom, voice control and other forms of assistive technology.
      </p>

      <h2>Our target is WCAG 2.2 AA</h2>
      <p>
        We target the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at Level AA. That is a target, not a certified
        audit. We have not commissioned an independent conformance audit and we do not claim full conformance or a
        VPAT. The <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/" rel="noopener">W3C WCAG 2.2 specification</a> is the
        reference we use when deciding whether a change improves or weakens access.
      </p>

      <h2>What has been implemented</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>One descriptive H1 on each page and a logical heading order for screen-reader navigation.</li>
        <li>Semantic landmarks, lists, tables and form-free links rather than image-based navigation.</li>
        <li>Keyboard-operable links and controls, with a visible focus indicator.</li>
        <li>Text and interface colours chosen for contrast against their backgrounds.</li>
        <li>Layouts that reflow at 200% browser zoom without two-dimensional page scrolling.</li>
        <li>No autoplay, no background video and no decorative motion that starts without the visitor.</li>
        <li>Alt text on informative images and text descriptions for the industrial schematics that replace product photographs.</li>
        <li>Tables with header cells and captions or explanatory text where a table needs context.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Schematic drawings and text alternatives</h2>
      <p>
        Product visuals on this site are industrial schematics, not photographs. Each drawing is accompanied by a
        description of the format, construction or print sequence it represents. The description is intended to
        carry the same buying information as the drawing; it does not pretend that an abstract line drawing is a
        photograph of a delivered job. If a schematic is the only way a page explains a point and its description is
        not enough, tell us and we will add a plain-text explanation.
      </p>

      <h2>Known limitations</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Wide tables.</strong> Some comparison tables need more width than a phone screen provides and scroll horizontally on small screens. The headings remain visible, but horizontal scrolling may be awkward with some assistive technology.</li>
        <li><strong>Technical drawings.</strong> The SVGs are drawings, not photographs. Their line weight and labels can be less useful than a photograph when someone needs to inspect a real surface or finish.</li>
        <li><strong>External sites.</strong> A link to a registry, standards body, carrier or authority takes you to a site we do not control and cannot audit.</li>
        <li><strong>Email and messaging clients.</strong> Quotations, proofs and replies sent by email or WhatsApp are outside this website and may have accessibility limitations in your client.</li>
        <li><strong>PDF and supplier documents.</strong> If we send a PDF, it may not be tagged or structured for screen readers, especially when it comes from a material supplier or carrier. Ask for the information in another format if needed.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How to report an accessibility barrier</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}?subject=Accessibility`}>{site.email}</a> with the subject
        <strong>Accessibility</strong>. Please include the page URL or document name, what you were trying to do,
        what went wrong, and the browser, device or assistive technology you used if you are willing to share it.
        A screenshot or the exact wording that failed helps us reproduce the issue. Tell us if you need the
        information in a different format, such as plain text or larger type.
      </p>

      <h2>Response and remediation</h2>
      <p>
        We aim to acknowledge an accessibility report within 10 business days. The acknowledgement will say whether
        we can reproduce the issue, what we propose to change and when we expect to update the page. If a fix needs
        a design change, we will give you the interim alternative we can provide. These times are targets for a
        small team, not a promise that every technical fix can be completed in the same period.
      </p>

      <h2>Review cadence</h2>
      <p>
        This statement and the page templates are reviewed annually and after a substantial redesign. We also review
        them when a reported barrier shows a pattern rather than a one-page mistake. The review date at the top of
        the page changes whenever this statement is substantively updated.
      </p>
      <p class="small">
        Related policies: <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> · <a href="/cookies/">Cookies</a> ·
        <a href="/terms/">Terms</a> · <a href="/refund-policy/">Returns</a> ·
        <a href="/shipping-delivery/">Shipping</a> · <a href="/declarations/">Declarations</a> ·
        <a href="/editorial-standards/">Editorial standards</a> · <a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a> ·
        <a href="/corrections/">Corrections</a> · <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> ·
        <a href="/contact/">Contact</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
